{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_research_key_rotation_teardown_notes_finding_a_base_port_endpoint_churn", "label": "Finding A \u2014 post-cutover device churn applies base-port endpoints to the offset-port tun", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/key-rotation-teardown-notes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "device_config_at_port rewrites peer endpoints to the offset port at bring-up, but every active-tun apply path recomputes device_config_pinned from primary_endpoint() (base port); the cutover change-guard seed masks it for the unchanged config, so only a legitimate post-cutover change silently black-holes the session."}, {"id": "docs_research_key_rotation_teardown_notes_finding_b_punch_binds_base_port", "label": "Finding B \u2014 post-rotation NAT re-punch binds the base (retired) port", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/key-rotation-teardown-notes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "PathCtx deliberately punches from base_wg_port because binding the active/offset port would let the punch socket steal the live new tun's inbound datagrams \u2014 correct for the no-rotation case, wrong after a cutover."}, {"id": "docs_research_key_rotation_teardown_notes_finding_c_process_local_retirement", "label": "Finding C \u2014 retirement is process-local; a reboot resurrects the retired epoch", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/key-rotation-teardown-notes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "FIXED for locally-cut-over rotations by Backlog 3 Task 1 (promote/retire persisted, select_boot_key). Residuals: the controller's rule-4 grace-promote is not reconciled into the store, and the epoch-0 key remains in identity.json/wg_private.key."}, {"id": "docs_research_key_rotation_teardown_notes_finding_d_role_b_cidr_churn", "label": "Finding D \u2014 Role-B post-cutover CIDR churn routes via wg0", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/key-rotation-teardown-notes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_key_rotation_teardown_notes_finding_e_rule4_promotes_dead_key", "label": "Finding E \u2014 a wrong-but-real epoch key does not fail safe (rule 4 promotes it)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/key-rotation-teardown-notes.md", "source_location": "rotation.rs:55-110", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The ack signal is an accelerator, never a veto: rule 2 is the only abort path and rule 4 promotes on the GRACE_PROMOTE timeout regardless of ack state, so a key nobody can use is promoted and the prior epoch retired \u2014 a wedged gateway with no component reporting an error."}, {"id": "docs_research_key_rotation_teardown_notes_role_b_collapse", "label": "maybe_collapse_role_b \u2014 reverse make-before-break collapse", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/key-rotation-teardown-notes.md", "source_location": "main.rs State arm", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_key_rotation_teardown_notes_select_boot_key", "label": "EpochKeys::select_boot_key", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/research/key-rotation-teardown-notes.md", "source_location": "crates/wiremesh-gateway/src/epochkeys.rs:172-187", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_research_key_rotation_teardown_notes_finding_a_base_port_endpoint_churn", "target": "docs_research_key_rotation_teardown_notes_finding_b_punch_binds_base_port", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/research/key-rot